BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Sleepledger) Tj T* () Tj T* (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY) Tj T* () Tj T* (Sleepledger, Inc. \(S Corp\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Shift workers do not sleep good. This is a well known problem that effects millions of workers) Tj T* (across America and the world. Nurses work night shifts, truck drivers drive at all hours,) Tj T* (factory workers rotate between days and nights, and all of them have fatigue. Fatigue can lead) Tj T* (to accidents, mistakes, health problems, and lower productivity. Occupational clinics, which) Tj T* (are the clinics that see workers for work related health matters, do not have a good way to) Tj T* (know how their patients are sleeping and so they cant give good recomendations. Right now the) Tj T* (clinics mostly just ask the worker how they have been sleeping and the worker says fine or not) Tj T* (fine. This is not data driven and is a big gap in the market that nobody is addressing in a) Tj T* (meaningful way.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Sleepledger is a web app that collects sleep and schedule data from shift workers and gives it) Tj T* (to occupational clinics so they can recommend personalized rest plans and spot fatigue risks) Tj T* (early. The worker goes to the website and types in what time they went to sleep, what time they) Tj T* (woke up, and what shifts they worked. Our system then does analytics on the data and produces a) Tj T* (score for each worker. The clinic has a dashboard where they can see all of there workers and) Tj T* (who has a high score. Then the clinic can make a rest plan for the worker. We believe this is a) Tj T* (holistic end to end solution that leverages the power of data to transform how fatigue is) Tj T* (managed. Our prototype MVP has been built and has the worker log page and a basic clinic page.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market Opportunity) Tj T* () Tj T* (The market for this is very large. There are many shift workers in the United States, probably) Tj T* (around 15 to 20 percent of all workers, which is tens of millions of people. There are also) Tj T* (thousands of occupational clinics. The sleep health market is growing every year and is) Tj T* (expected to be worth many billions of dollars. If we only capture a small percent of this) Tj T* (market we will be very succesful. We have not done a formal market study yet but we are) Tj T* (confident the numbers are big. Our target customers are occupational clinics first, and later) Tj T* (we may also go after employers, hospitals, trucking companies, and maybe insurance companies) Tj T* (and even individual consumers who want to track there sleep.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our business model has a few options and we are still deciding which is best. One option is) Tj T* (that clinics pay a monthly subscription for the dashboard. Another option is that workers pay a) Tj T* (small fee to use the app. A third option is that employers pay for the whole thing for there) Tj T* (workers. We might also sell the data and analytics to other companies, or charge for a) Tj T* (consulting service where we help clinics set up the rest plans. We think a mix of these will) Tj T* (work and will decide when we talk to more customers. Pricing has not been decided yet but it) Tj T* (would be somewhere between a low and medium price per month. Over time we expect revenue to) Tj T* (grow as more clinics and workers join the platform.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are many sleep trackers and wearables on the market, as well as sleep apps, but these are) Tj T* (mostly for regular consumers and not for shift workers and clinics. Some big companies make) Tj T* (smart watches that track sleep automatically. We think we are different because we focus on) Tj T* (shift workers and clinics and combine the sleep with the work schedule. We do not think any) Tj T* (competitor does exactly what we do, although we have not searched very thoroughly. Our) Tj T* (advantage is that we understand the problem and are first to this specific niche. Large) Tj T* (companies could copy us, but we believe we can move faster because we are a small and agile) Tj ET
endstream
