BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (team.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Brandon Teller is the CEO and is a senior at our university studying business. He came up with) Tj T* (the idea after his uncle, who is a night shift worker, said he was always tired. Brandon is in) Tj T* (charge of strategy, sales, and the vision of the company.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Kiara Oduya-Whitfield is the head of product and is a junior studying psychology with a minor) Tj T* (in health sciences. She has an interest in sleep and has read many articles about it. She is) Tj T* (responsible for the user experience and for the content of the rest plans.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marcus Delvecchio is the CTO and is a sophomore studying computer science. He built the) Tj T* (prototype MVP over a few months and is responsible for the website and all the technical parts) Tj T* (including the analytics.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We do not currently have a clinician or a sleep doctor on the team, but we plan to find an) Tj T* (advisor in the future.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have defined our core business concept, formed our legal entity as an S Corp, built a) Tj T* (prototype MVP, and launched a website. We have not yet had any paying customers or any clinics) Tj T* (using the product. We have shown the prototype to a few friends and family members, who said it) Tj T* (looks good. We have not yet run a pilot. We have not yet had any revenue, and our expenses so) Tj T* (far have been small, mostly the cost of forming the company and the website hosting, which the) Tj T* (founders paid for themselves.) Tj T* () Tj T* (For financials, we project that in year one we will have a small number of clinics and some) Tj T* (revenue, and that by year three we will have grown to many clinics and be profitable. We have) Tj T* (not built a detailed financial model yet, but we believe the growth will be rapid because the) Tj T* (market is so big. Our main costs will be software development, marketing, and eventually hiring) Tj T* (staff. We expect to break even at some point once we have enough customers.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are asking for prize money from the competition to help us take Sleepledger to the next) Tj T* (level. We would use the funds for further development of the product, marketing, and finding) Tj T* (our first clinic customers. We would also like to get mentorship and connections to people in) Tj T* (the health industry and investors, since we do not have much experience in healthcare. Any) Tj T* (amount would be helpful, but a larger amount would let us hire a developer and do a real pilot.) Tj T* (We also would like advice on privacy and regulation, since we know health data can be sensitive) Tj T* (and there are laws but we are not sure exactly which ones apply to us.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Conclusion) Tj T* () Tj T* (Sleepledger has the potential to change how fatigue is managed for shift workers everywhere.) Tj T* (With a huge market, a passionate team, and a working prototype, we believe we are well) Tj T* (positioned to succeed and to make a real difference in peoples lives. We thank the judges for) Tj T* (there time and consideration.) Tj ET
endstream
